 made for some industries or individuals with essential jobs. Housewives became key players in conserving food, encouraged to cook with substitutes and avoid waste. Victory gardens and “Meatless Mondays” became symbols of homefront patriotism. While the program faced complaints and black-market activity, it was generally respected and helped the US sustain a long and resource-consuming global conflict."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectHandCardNotifyText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"6FD815B347B42428343F18B7AAA41DA3","SourceString":"Chosen card must have Bond.","LocalizedString":"Chosen card must have Bond."},"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","chooseOneCards":[{"cardText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"63BE9DDB4E1A8076608036A6E9A5B20C","SourceString":"Remove Bond from all cards in your hand.","LocalizedString":"Remove Bond from all cards in your hand."},"selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":false},{"cardText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"648616FD4954510125E95AB57FD4CC9D","SourceString":"Give your HQ +4 defense.","LocalizedString":"Give your HQ +4 defense."},"selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":false}],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/10_Homefront/T_rationing.T_rationing","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/RATIONING.RATIONING","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_rationing_photo","SourceString":"A young boy using a War Ration Book to purchase a can of vegetables, February 1943.","LocalizedString":"A young boy using a War Ration Book to purchase a can of vegetables, February 1943."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isAttackBuff":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"count","type":"int32","dire